quran[19]{c,v,t}:
  73,1,O mantled (Beloved!)
  73,2,"Rise and stand (in Prayer) at night but (for) a short while,"
  73,3,"Half the night or decrease it a little,"
  73,4,Or increase a little more to it. And recite the Qur’an with most pleasant pauses.
  73,5,Soon We shall send down to you a burdensome command.
  73,6,"No doubt rising at night strictly subdues (the ill-commanding self), and makes the tongue deliver straight and clear speech (with the concentration of head and heart)."
  73,7,"Of course, there are many commitments for you during the day."
  73,8,"And continue remembering the Name of your Lord, devoted completely to Him alone (in your heart and soul), broken away from everyone else."
  73,9,He is the Lord of the east and the west. There is no God but He. So take Him alone as (your) Guardian.
  73,10,And observe patience with what they (disbelievers) utter and turn aside from them in a fine manner.
  73,11,And leave Me (to deal) with the denying rich money-mongers (to take revenge). And give them a little respite (so that their evil deeds may cross the limit).
  73,12,"Surely, We have heavy shackles and the Blazing Fire (of Hell),"
  73,13,And food that chokes the throat and most painful torment.
  73,14,The Day when the earth and the mountains shall shake violently and mountains will turn into heaps of flying away sand.
  73,15,"Surely, We have sent towards you a Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) who bears witness to you (seeing thoroughly your states of being) as We sent a Messenger towards Pharaoh."
  73,16,"So Pharaoh disobeyed that Messenger, and We seized him with a devastating seizure."
  73,17,"If you continue disbelieving, then how will you save yourselves from (the torment of) that Day which will turn the children old,"
  73,18,(The Day) by whose severity the heaven will be split apart? His promise is bound to be fulfilled.
  73,19,"Verily, this (Qur’an) is an admonition. So let him who desires adopt the way to reach his Lord."
